759 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 621 0 R
/E (Liver cirrhosis is a health concern. It causes damage to liver cells scarring and impairs liver function. People are searching for safer treatments from natural sources. This is because they want to avoid harm from existing treatments.Pergularia daemia is a plant used in traditional medicine. Researchers studied it for its potential to protect the liver. They wanted to see if it could help prevent liver damage.The study tested the plant extract on liver cells in a lab. They checked what good stuff is in the plant. Liver cells were damaged with an agent. Then they were treated with amounts of the plant extract. A known protective compound, diosgenin was used for comparison.The study checked how well the extract protected the cells. They looked at cell survival leakage of liver enzymes and stress levels. The plant extract helped cells survive and reduced enzyme leakage. This happened in a step-by-step manner as the amount of extract increased. The extract also reduced stress showing it can act as an antioxidant. Its effects were similar to the compound, at some concentrations.The vitro evaluation of hepatoprotective activity is really important for finding new treatments for liver problems. Pergularia daemia is a plant that people have used for a time in traditional medicine. It has good properties, especially when it comes to fighting antioxidants and inflammation. This study looks at whether Pergularia daemia extract can protect liver cells from damage.The plant extract was made using a method to get the good stuff out like flavonoids, alkaloids and phenolic compounds. Liver cells were then hurt on purpose. We checked if the extract could protect them.We used a test called MTT assay to see how many cells were still alive. We found that more cells survived when they were treated with the extract. The extract also reduced stress in the cells by lowering reactive oxygen species levels and stopping lipid peroxidation.The extract helped the cells defend themselves better by increasing enzyme activities. When we looked at the cells under a microscope we saw that the treated cells looked normal. The untreated cells were damaged.The levels of biochemicals like ALT and AST went back to normal after treatment. This shows that the extract protected the liver cells. The extract also reduced inflammation by lowering cytokine production. It even minimized DNA damage and cell death in liver cells. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
