/E (Some studies have indicated its potential in reducing inflammation-related liver damage and improving overall cellular function. However, most of the existing research is limited to preliminary or in-vivo studies, with relatively few investigations focusing on in-vitro hepatocyte models. This gap in the literature highlights the need for more comprehensive studies to evaluate the hepatoprotective activity of Pergularia daemia under controlled laboratory conditions. The present study aims to address this gap by providing detailed in-vitro evidence of its protective effects, thereby contributing to the growing body of knowledge on plant-based )
