/E (Although Pergularia daemia has been traditionally used for the treatment of liver-related ailments, scientific validation of its hepatoprotective activity remains insufficient, particularly in controlled in-vitro settings. Most of the existing studies focus on general pharmacological properties such as anti-inflammatory or antimicrobial effects, with only a few addressing its role in liver protection. Moreover, the available research is largely based on in-vivo animal models, which, while useful, do not provide detailed insights at the cellular level. In-vitro studies using hepatocyte cell lines are essential for understanding the direct )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [6]
