/E (Another important research gap is the lack of standardized extraction methods and dosage optimization for Pergularia daemia. Variations in plant collection, extraction techniques, and experimental conditions can lead to inconsistent results, making it difficult to compare findings across different studies. Additionally, there is limited information on the optimal concentration of the plant extract required to achieve maximum hepatoprotective activity without causing toxicity. Establishing standardized protocols for extraction and determining the effective dose range are essential steps for ensuring reproducibility and reliability in research. Furthermore, dose-dependent studies are necessary to understand the relationship between concentration and biological response, which is critical for potential therapeutic applications. Addressing this gap will contribute to the development of more consistent and scientifically validated data, supporting the future use of Pergularia daemia in liver disease management. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
