/E (The crude extract of Pergularia daemia was subjected to preliminary qualitative phytochemical screening to identify the presence of important secondary metabolites. Standard phytochemical tests were carried out for the detection of alkaloids, flavonoids, tannins, saponins, glycosides, phenols, terpenoids, and steroids using established laboratory procedures. The appearance of characteristic colour changes or precipitates was recorded as an indication of the presence of the respective phytochemical constituents \(Devi et al., 2021\). This analysis was performed to obtain preliminary information on the bioactive compounds that may contribute to the hepatoprotective activity of the plant extract. )
/Pg 39 0 R
