/P 649 0 R
/E (Preliminary phytochemical screening of the crude extract of Pergularia daemia revealed the presence of several important secondary metabolites such as flavonoids, alkaloids, saponins, glycosides, phenols, and terpenoids. These phytoconstituents are known to possess antioxidant and cytoprotective properties, which may contribute to the hepatoprotective activity of the plant extract. The presence of these compounds supports the traditional medicinal use of the plant and provides a scientific basis for its biological activity. )
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [18]
>>
