1534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 655 0 R
/E (The hepatoprotective activity observed in this study can be attributed to multiple underlying mechanisms. The primary mechanism appears to be the antioxidant action of the plant extract, which reduces oxidative stress by scavenging reactive oxygen species. This is supported by the significant decrease in ROS and MDA levels observed in treated groups \(Tables 3 and 4\). Additionally, the reduction in ALT and AST levels \(Table 2\) suggests stabilization of cell membranes and prevention of enzyme leakage. This indicates that the extract helps maintain structural integrity and protects hepatocytes from damage. The improvement in cell viability \(Table 1\) further confirms the cytoprotective effect of the extract, which may involve the activation of cellular repair pathways and inhibition of apoptosis. Together, these mechanisms highlight the multifaceted nature of hepatoprotection provided by Pergularia daemia and emphasize its potential therapeutic value. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
