/Title (help protect hepatocytes from damage and maintain cellular integrity \(Prakash et al., 2022; Sun et al., 2022\). In addition to its antioxidant activity, the plant has been reported to possess anti- inflammatory and cytoprotective effects, which further contribute to its potential hepatoprotective action \(Prakash et al., 2022\). Traditional knowledge regarding its use in liver disorders provides a valuable foundation for scientific validation. Evaluating the hepatoprotective activity of Pergularia daemia through controlled in-vitro studies not only helps in understanding its mechanism of action but also supports its potential development as a natural therapeutic agent for liver diseases such as cirrhosis.)
